    "content": "{\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"content\": \"#include \\\"knn.h\\\"\\n#include <arm_neon.h>\\n#include <omp.h>\\n#include <float.h>\\n\\n// Max-heap node (1-indexed) with global point index for tie-breaking\\ntypedef struct {\\n    float dist;\\n    char label;\\n    int idx;   // global point index in input order\\n} HeapNode;\\n\\nstatic inline void heap_swap(HeapNode *a, HeapNode *b) {\\n    HeapNode t = *a; *a = *b; *b = t;\\n}\\n\\n// Sift down from index idx in a max-heap of size heap_size (1-indexed)\\n// Compare distance first, then global index for tie-breaking.\\nstatic inline void sift_down(HeapNode *heap, int heap_size, int idx) {\\n    while (1) {\\n        int largest = idx;\\n        int left = 2 * idx;\\n        int right = 2 * idx + 1;\\n        if (left <= heap_size &&\\n            (heap[left].dist > heap[largest].dist ||\\n             (heap[left].dist == heap[largest].dist && heap[left].idx < heap[largest].idx)))\\n            largest = left;\\n        if (right <= heap_size &&\\n            (heap[right].dist > heap[largest].dist ||\\n             (heap[right].dist == heap[largest].dist && heap[right].idx < heap[largest].idx)))\\n            largest = right;\\n        if (largest == idx) break;\\n        heap_swap(&heap[idx], &heap[largest]);\\n        idx = largest;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n// Insert or replace in a max-heap of capacity k.\\n// *heap_size_ptr is current number of elements; after call it may increase up to k.\\nstatic inline void heap_insert_or_replace(float d, char label, int global_idx,\\n                                          HeapNode *heap, int *heap_size_ptr, int k) {\\n    int hs = *heap_size_ptr;\\n    if (hs < k) {\\n        // Insert at end and bubble up\\n        hs++;\\n        int idx = hs;\\n        heap[idx].dist = d;\\n        heap[idx].label = label;\\n        heap[idx].idx = global_idx;\\n        while (idx > 1 &&\\n               (heap[idx / 2].dist < heap[idx].dist ||\\n                (heap[idx / 2].dist == heap[idx].dist && heap[idx / 2].idx > heap[idx].idx))) {\\n            heap_swap(&heap[idx], &heap[idx / 2]);\\n            idx /= 2;\\n        }\\n    } else if (d < heap[1].dist ||\\n               (d == heap[1].dist && global_idx < heap[1].idx)) {\\n        // Replace root\\n        heap[1].dist = d;\\n        heap[1].label = label;\\n        heap[1].idx = global_idx;\\n        sift_down(heap, k, 1);\\n    }\\n    *heap_size_ptr = hs;\\n}\\n\\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group *groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\\n    // Precompute start index for each group (global point order)\\n    int *start_idx = (int *)malloc(n_groups * sizeof(int));\\n    int total_points = 0;\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\\n        start_idx[i] = total_points;\\n        total_points += groups[i].length;\\n    }\\n\\n    // Determine number of threads once (outside parallel region)\\n    int max_threads = omp_get_max_threads();\\n    if (max_threads < 1) max_threads = 1;\\n\\n    // Per-thread heaps: each thread gets a heap array of size k+1 and its current size.\\n    HeapNode **thread_heaps = (HeapNode**) malloc(max_threads * sizeof(HeapNode*));\\n    int *thread_sizes = (int*) calloc(max_threads, sizeof(int));\\n\\n    for (int t = 0; t < max_threads; t++) {\\n        thread_heaps[t] = (HeapNode*) malloc((k + 1) * sizeof(HeapNode));\\n        // Initialize with sentinel values: large distance and invalid label/index.\\n        for (int i = 1; i <= k; i++) {\\n            thread_heaps[t][i].dist = FLT_MAX;\\n            thread_heaps[t][i].label = -1;\\n            thread_heaps[t][i].idx = -1;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    #pragma omp parallel\\n    {\\n        int tid = omp_get_thread_num();\\n        HeapNode *local_heap = thread_heaps[tid];\\n        int local_size = 0;   // persistent across groups assigned to this thread\\n\\n        #pragma omp for schedule(guided)\\n        for (int gi = 0; gi < n_groups; gi++) {\\n            Group g = groups[gi];\\n            float *xs = g.xs;\\n            float *ys = g.ys;\\n            int len = g.length;\\n            char label = g.label;\\n            int base_idx = start_idx[gi];   // global index of first point in this group\\n\\n            // Process points in batches of 16 using NEON SIMD (vld1q_f32_x4)\\n            int j = 0;\\n            for (; j + 15 < len; j += 16) {\\n                float32x4x4_t x_vec_quad = vld1q_f32_x4(xs + j);\\n                float32x4x4_t y_vec_quad = vld1q_f32_x4(ys + j);\\n\\n                float tx = to_evaluate.x;\\n                float ty = to_evaluate.y;\\n\\n                // Compute distances for each of the four vectors\\n                float32x4_t dx0 = vsubq_f32(x_vec_quad.val[0], vdupq_n_f32(tx));\\n                float32x4_t dy0 = vsubq_f32(y_vec_quad.val[0], vdupq_n_f32(ty));\\n                float32x4_t dist_sq0 = vmlaq_f32(vmulq_f32(dx0, dx0), dy0, dy0);\\n\\n                float32x4_t dx1 = vsubq_f32(x_vec_quad.val[1], vdupq_n_f32(tx));\\n                float32x4_t dy1 = vsubq_f32(y_vec_quad.val[1], vdupq_n_f32(ty));\\n                float32x4_t dist_sq1 = vmlaq_f32(vmulq_f32(dx1, dx1), dy1, dy1);\\n\\n                float32x4_t dx2 = vsubq_f32(x_vec_quad.val[2], vdupq_n_f32(tx));\\n                float32x4_t dy2 = vsubq_f32(y_vec_quad.val[2], vdupq_n_f32(ty));\\n                float32x4_t dist_sq2 = vmlaq_f32(vmulq_f32(dx2, dx2), dy2, dy2);\\n\\n                float32x4_t dx3 = vsubq_f32(x_vec_quad.val[3], vdupq_n_f32(tx));\\n                float32x4_t dy3 = vsubq_f32(y_vec_quad.val[3], vdupq_n_f32(ty));\\n                float32x4_t dist_sq3 = vmlaq_f32(vmulq_f32(dx3, dx3), dy3, dy3);\\n\\n                // Store all 16 distances\\n                float d[16];\\n                vst1q_f32(d,     dist_sq0);\\n                vst1q_f32(d + 4, dist_sq1);\\n                vst1q_f32(d + 8, dist_sq2);\\n                vst1q_f32(d+12, dist_sq3);\\n\\n                // Insert all 16 distances into heap (unrolled loop)\\n                for (int t = 0; t < 16; t++) {\\n                    int global_idx = base_idx + j + t;\\n                    heap_insert_or_replace(d[t], label, global_idx,\\n                                           local_heap, &local_size, k);\\n                }\\n            }\\n\\n            // Scalar remainder\\n            for (; j < len; j++) {\\n                Point p;\\n                p.x = xs[j];\\n                p.y = ys[j];\\n                float d = euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(to_evaluate, p);\\n                int global_idx = base_idx + j;\\n                heap_insert_or_replace(d, label, global_idx,\\n                                       local_heap, &local_size, k);\\n            }\\n        }\\n\\n        // Store final size for this thread after all its groups are processed\\n        thread_sizes[tid] = local_size;\\n    }\\n\\n    // Global max-heap to merge per-thread results\\n    HeapNode *global_heap = (HeapNode*) malloc((k + 1) * sizeof(HeapNode));\\n    for (int i = 1; i <= k; i++) {\\n        global_heap[i].dist = FLT_MAX;\\n        global_heap[i].label = -1;\\n        global_heap[i].idx = -1;\\n    }\\n    int global_size = 0;\\n\\n    // Merge all per-thread heaps into the global heap\\n    for (int t = 0; t < max_threads; t++) {\\n        HeapNode *local = thread_heaps[t];\\n        int sz = thread_sizes[t];\\n        if (sz > k) sz = k;\\n        for (int i = 1; i <= sz; i++) {\\n            heap_insert_or_replace(local[i].dist, local[i].label, local[i].idx,\\n                                   global_heap, &global_size, k);\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    // Extract labels from the final global heap into a plain array for frequency counting.\\n    char *labels = (char*) malloc(k * sizeof(char));\\n    int actual_k = (global_size < k) ? global_size : k;\\n    for (int i = 0; i < actual_k; i++) {\\n        labels[i] = global_heap[i + 1].label;\\n    }\\n    // Fill remaining with -1 if not enough points\\n    for (int i = actual_k; i < k; i++) {\\n        labels[i] = -1;\\n    }\\n\\n    free(global_heap);\\n    for (int t = 0; t < max_threads; t++) {\\n        free(thread_heaps[t]);\\n    }\\n    free(thread_heaps);\\n    free(thread_sizes);\\n    free(start_idx);\\n\\n    // Find most frequent label using frequency array (O(k + 256))\\n    int freq[256] = {0};\\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\\n        if (labels[i] >= 0)\\n            freq[(unsigned char)labels[i]]++;\\n    }\\n\\n    char best_label = labels[0];\\n    int best_count = freq[(unsigned char)best_label];\\n    for (int c = 1; c < 256; c++) {\\n        if (freq[c] > best_count) {\\n            best_count = freq[c];\\n            best_label = (char)c;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    free(labels);\\n    return best_label;\\n}\\n\\nint main() {\\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\\n\\n    Group *groups = (Group *)malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\\n\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; ++i) {\\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\\n    }\\n\\n    int k = parse_k();\\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\\n\\n    printf(\\\"%c\\\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\\n}\\n\",\n      \"path\": \"src/knn.c\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Integrating all three archived transformations: (A) max-heap top-k selection with frequency-array counting and direct iteration over groups without copying, (B) SoA storage for coordinates and NEON SIMD distance computation using batch size 16 via vld1q_f32_x4 plus a scalar remainder, and (C) OpenMP parallelization with guided schedule, per-thread heaps allocated once outside the parallel region, and global point index tie-breaking during heap insertion to ensure deterministic behavior when distances are equal will yield a correct program that is faster than any single transformation. The combination exploits SIMD parallelism for distance computation, reduces memory latency through SoA layout, uses efficient max-heap insertion per thread to maintain the k nearest neighbors without sorting, distributes work across threads using guided schedule for load balancing, and guarantees exact tie-breaking matching sequential baseline order via global indices.\",\n  \"notes\": \"Changed schedule from static to guided (source C). Added int idx field to HeapNode struct. Precomputed start_idx array for deterministic global point ordering. Modified heap_insert_or_replace and sift_down to compare distances first, then global index when equal. This ensures that among points with identical distance, the one appearing earlier in input order is preferred, matching baseline behavior under parallel execution.\",\n  \"sources_kept\": [\n    \"8aad4586faad45a1\",\n    \"74722b26180e4b94\",\n    \"a30843e46bab4973\"\n  ],\n  \"transformations\": [\n    \"Eliminate flattening arrays (A)\",\n    \"Direct iteration over groups without copying (A)\",\n    \"Replace qsort with frequency array for final label selection (A)\",\n    \"Restructure Group storage from Point* points to separate float* xs, float* ys (SoA) (B)\",\n    \"Use ARM NEON intrinsics vld1q_f32/vsubq_f32/vmulq_f32/vmlaq_f32 for batched distance computation with batch size 16 via vld1q_f32_x4 (B)\",\n    \"Factor heap insertion into static inline helper function (B)\",\n    \"OpenMP parallelization over groups (C)\",\n    \"Guided schedule for load balancing (C)\",\n    \"Thread-local storage: per-thread heaps allocated once outside parallel region (C)\",\n    \"Merge with global point index tie-breaking to ensure deterministic selection when distances are equal (C)\"\n  ]\n}",
